      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_3869651f",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: theyre_in_a_relationship_who_makes_the_sandwiches; hasOverallIntent: mysogynous; overall-intent-description: The image shows two women holding hands and smiling against a pink background. The text overlay reads, \"they're in a relationship, who makes the sandwiches?\" This meme uses a common sexist trope that implies women are expected to handle domestic chores like making sandwiches, thereby reinforcing traditional gender roles. The intent is to humorously or sarcastically suggest that in a relationship, one partner (typically assumed to be the woman) is expected to take on the domestic labor, which is a form of mysogynous content as it perpetuates the stereotype that women are naturally responsible for household tasks.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_433b6204"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
