    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_fcccef2a",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target community for this meme is individuals who are familiar with and may find humor in traditional gender role stereotypes, particularly those who recognize the misogynous trope that women are expected to handle domestic chores like making sandwiches. The meme is likely intended for a general online audience that understands and engages with internet humor that critiques or satirizes outdated gender norms, often through sarcasm or irony. The visual of two women holding hands and smiling against a pink background may also appeal to audiences interested in LGBTQ+ relationships or gender equality discussions, as the meme uses the image of a same-sex couple to highlight the persistence of gendered expectations in relationships. The meme’s humor relies on the audience’s awareness of the stereotype that women 'belong in the kitchen,' making it most effective for those who have encountered or recognize this cultural reference.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_433b6204"
      },
